 reviewer, owning 100% of grouped_exposure.rb. It does not give Kochnev's 62-76% share of the directory and does not say no active person is an expert there. It presents Marco as a real owner, not a stand-in.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A says Lena Brandt is the only active contributor with about 11% of the delegator code. Kochnev has 66.7%, below the 68-82% band. An active person, Lena, is credited with ownership, so it fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (143 lines) instead of mostly Kochnev. It does not give Marco's repo-wide share and does not mention Anna's patch correctly. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Lena with 18 lines in exposure and treats her as the second reviewer. It gives no departed share of 79-90% and no Scholz/Subbota split. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B says dblock has the most commits (about 112) and that Kochnev has the most lines. It gives no commit or line percentages and does not state dblock's 5.6% share. It does not meet the numeric bands, and it does not merge Doubrovkine's spellings fully.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B recommends Marco Silva as the primary reviewer with 147 lines and says Kochnev's 493 lines are about 3.4 times Marco's. It does not say Kochnev wrote 62-76% of exposure or that active people own at most 8%. It treats Marco as a reviewer, though not a deep owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco with owning lines in the delegator area, based on the rename. It does not follow the delegators back to Kochnev's 75% and does not state that no active person owns any line.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Marco with 147 surviving lines in exposure and delegator, including GroupedExposure, which is far above the 2% repo limit and treats copied code as Marco's. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Lena with 30 lines and offers her as a second reviewer. It gives no departed share. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C says that in exposure the top committer and the top line owner are the same person, Kochnev. Across the repo, it says dblock has the most commits but does not give line shares or compare dblock's lines to Kochnev's. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C says Kochnev has about half of exposure and recommends Marco Silva with 143 lines as the primary reviewer. It does not say no active person is an expert and does not give Kochnev's 69%. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives Kochnev 59% of the delegator code, below the 68-82% band. It names Lena and Marco as owners of 10 and 4 of 102 lines, which credits active people with ownership. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Marco with 143 surviving lines in exposure and treats him as the primary reviewer. It does not credit grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Lena as a backup reviewer with 20 lines. It gives no departed share and does not separate Scholz from Subbota. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D says dblock has the most commits (18.2%) with 10.4% of lines, and Kochnev has 18.7% of lines and left in 2015. The shares are outside the bands: dblock at 10.4% is above 8%, Kochnev at 18.7% is below 21%, and the commit share of 18.2% is below 28%. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Kochnev 54% of exposure, below the 62-76% band. Marco's 19% of exposure comes from grouped_exposure.rb, and active people hold 19.9%, above the 8% limit. It recommends Marco for that file, although it caveats this. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Kochnev 71% of the delegator code, in band, but credits Marco Silva with 4.1% and calls him the reviewer. He is the only active person to have touched it, but the criterion requires nobody active to own any line (0%). Not met.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D credits Marco with 117 lines of grouped_exposure.rb and about 2.6% of the repo when merged. That is over 2%, and it attributes grouped_exposure.rb to Marco, not to Kochnev. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D says 89.3% of lines belong to people with no recent commit, which is in the 79-90% band. It does not discuss Lena's headers, bots, or the Scholz/Subbota split in the way the criterion requires, and Scholz's lines are cited at 7.9%. It fails overall.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E says dblock has the most commits but only about 34 lines, and Kochnev has about 756 lines in lib/. It gives no percentages in the required bands and does not merge dblock's aliases into a figure. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E names Lena Brandt first for exposure. It does not give Kochnev's share of the directory, and it treats Lena, Anna and Marco as the only active reviewers, with the caveat that they are thin. It does not meet the numeric requirements.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E names Marco and then Lena as delegator reviewers. It gives no Kochnev share and does not say that nobody active owns any line.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco with 143 lines in lib/, which is far more than 2%. It does not address grouped_exposure.rb or Anna's patch. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives no departed share and makes Lena a main reviewer. It does not discuss mechanical lines, bots, or the Scholz/Subbota split correctly. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F says Doubrovkine has the most commits (about 117 across variants) and that Kochnev owns the most code (758 lines in lib/) and left in 2015. It gives no percentages and does not state Doubrovkine's share of lines. It fails the numeric bands.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F calls Marco Silva the only active person with substantial surviving code there, with 147 lines. It says Kochnev wrote most of it but gives no 62-76% figure and no statement that active people own at most 8%. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco for the delegator code after the rename, and it counts his 147 lines against exposure and delegator together. It does not state Kochnev's 75% or that no active person owns any line.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Marco with 147 lines in exposure and delegator, which is not a repo-wide share under 2% and makes him look like an owner. It admits the counts may be inflated. It does not attribute grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Lena Brandt with 30 surviving lines and offers her as a backup reviewer. It gives no departed share. It fails.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":18636,"type":"result","duration_ms":18647,"uuid":"b49cc37a-1331-46c9-a61e-49696bd49554","ttft_stream_ms":1918,"time_to_request_ms":413,"first_content_frame_ms":1918,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
